---
import { ArrowLeft, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro'
import TechBookPlan from '../../components/TechBookPlan.astro'
import { site } from '../../config/site'
import { techbookResources } from '../../config/techbook'
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---
<Layout title="TechBook | The Lab | Vicus Brits" description="Explore TechBook, a practical experiment in AI-assisted software engineering and its project resources.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="techbook-hero" aria-labelledby="techbook-title">
      <div class="container">
        <a class="techbook-back" href="/#lab"><ArrowLeft size={18} aria-hidden="true" /> Back to The Lab</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE LAB / EXPERIMENT 01</p>
        <h1 id="techbook-title">TechBook<span>.</span></h1>
        <p class="techbook-lead">AI is making software easier to build. But is it making software better engineered?</p>
        <div class="body-copy techbook-overview">
          <p>TechBook is the first Lab project: a practical experiment exploring how one person can use AI to build software while maintaining clarity, control, understanding and trust.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section techbook-phase-overview" aria-label="TechBook engineering phases">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="techbook-phase-nav" aria-label="Explore the four TechBook phases">
          <a href="#define"><span>01</span> DEFINE</a>
          <a href="#design"><span>02</span> DESIGN</a>
          <a href="#deliver"><span>03</span> DELIVER</a>
          <a href="#defend"><span>04</span> DEFEND</a>
        </nav>

        <section class="techbook-phase techbook-phase-define" id="define" aria-labelledby="define-title">
          <p class="eyebrow">PHASE 01 / DEFINE</p>
          <h2 id="define-title">Human First.<br />AI in the Loop.</h2>
          <p class="techbook-phase-lead">From business intent to independently assured requirements.</p>
          <p>The first phase of the TechBook LAB explored a fundamental question: <em>Can AI agents define detailed software requirements without taking control of the business decisions?</em></p>
          <p>Rather than asking AI to simply build an application, we followed a structured <strong>12-step requirements process</strong>, using three specialist AI agents and three human approval gates.</p>

          <h3>How we did it</h3>
          <p>We started with a human-defined business problem: a technician-booking solution for a technical services company, including web-based booking, technician coordination and AI-assisted WhatsApp interactions.</p>
          <p>Three AI agents supported the process:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/research-agent/"><strong>Research Agent</strong></a> — Investigated five existing field-service platforms using a six-step research method: Plan, Discover, Investigate, Compare, Verify and Synthesize. Findings were supported by an evidence register rather than treated as unquestioned facts.</li>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/requirements-agent/"><strong>Requirements Agent</strong></a> — Followed the 12-step process, turning human intent and research into business scenarios, detailed requirements and measurable acceptance criteria. Where decisions were unclear, the agent proposed options for human approval.</li>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/requirements-assurance-agent/"><strong>Requirements Assurance Agent</strong></a> — Independently challenged the specification for completeness, consistency, security, traceability and testability. Findings were corrected by the Requirements Agent and independently rechecked.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Three human approval gates</h3>
          <ul class="techbook-gates">
            <li><strong>Gate 1 — Business Intent:</strong> Are we solving the right problem?</li>
            <li><strong>Gate 2 — Business Validation:</strong> Does the specification describe how the business should operate?</li>
            <li><strong>Gate 3 — Requirements Baseline:</strong> Is the specification sufficiently assured and controlled to proceed to Design?</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Throughout the process, AI researched, proposed, documented and challenged. <strong>The human retained authority over scope, business rules, risk acceptance and approvals.</strong></p>

          <h3>The resulting artifacts</h3>
          <p>The Define phase produced nine business scenarios, 26 requirements and 39 acceptance criteria, organised into three core documents:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/business-intent/"><strong>Business Intent Brief</strong></a> — The human-approved problem, scope, constraints and success measures.</li>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/requirements-specification/"><strong>Requirements Specification</strong></a> — The detailed, testable definition of TechBook.</li>
            <li><a href="/lab/techbook/requirements-decision-assurance-log/"><strong>Decision &amp; Assurance Log</strong></a> — The record of decisions, assurance findings, approvals and outstanding risks.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The supporting <a href="/lab/techbook/market-research/"><strong>Market Research</strong></a> provides the external evidence behind the discovery work.</p>
          <p><strong>Outcome:</strong> An independently reviewed requirements baseline, approved for Design, with unresolved technical feasibility risks explicitly recorded for subsequent verification.</p>
          <p>The experiment demonstrated a disciplined division of responsibility:</p>
          <p class="techbook-phase-principle"><strong>Human defines → AI researches and specifies → AI independently challenges → Human approves.</strong></p>

          <h3>Read the full story</h3>
          <p>For a detailed walkthrough of the 12-step process, how the agents collaborated, the human approval gates and the actual documents produced, read the Substack article:</p>
          <p><a class="techbook-story-link" href="https://vicusbrits.substack.com/p/the-ai-didnt-decide-what-to-build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>The AI Didn't Decide What to Build. We Did.</strong><ArrowUpRight size={18} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
          <p><em>The next LAB phase, DESIGN, explores how specialist agents turn these requirements into a solution architecture.</em></p>
        </section>

        <div class="techbook-phase-next">
          <section class="techbook-phase" id="design" aria-labelledby="design-title">
            <p class="eyebrow">PHASE 02</p>
            <h2 id="design-title">DESIGN<span>.</span></h2>
            <p>The Architecture Agent turns an approved requirements baseline into a human-governed solution design, investigates feasibility and makes technology choices visible before implementation.</p>
            <p><a href="/lab/techbook/architecture-agent/">Read the Architecture Agent instructions</a></p>
          </section>

          <section class="techbook-phase" id="deliver" aria-labelledby="deliver-title">
            <p class="eyebrow">PHASE 03</p>
            <h2 id="deliver-title">DELIVER<span>.</span></h2>
          </section>

          <section class="techbook-phase" id="defend" aria-labelledby="defend-title">
            <p class="eyebrow">PHASE 04</p>
            <h2 id="defend-title">DEFEND<span>.</span></h2>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section techbook-section" id="resources" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">PROJECT ARTEFACTS</p>
        <h2 id="resources-title">Resource library.</h2>
        <p class="body-copy techbook-intro">Documents, diagrams and AI skills will be shared here as they become available.</p>
        <div class="techbook-resource-grid">
          {techbookResources.map((category) => (
            <section class="techbook-resource" aria-labelledby={`resource-${category.title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}`}>
              <h3 id={`resource-${category.title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}`}>{category.title}</h3>
              {category.resources.length > 0 ? (
                <ul>
                  {category.resources.map((resource) => (
                    <li>
                      <a href={resource.url}>{resource.name}</a>
                      <p>{resource.description}</p>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              ) : <p>Coming soon.</p>}
            </section>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <TechBookPlan />
    <section class="section techbook-section" id="articles" aria-labelledby="articles-title">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE LAB &middot; TECHBOOK</p>
        <h2 id="articles-title">Articles.</h2>
        <article class="writing-card featured-article" aria-labelledby="techbook-article-title">
          <h3 id="techbook-article-title">Define. Design. Deliver. Defend | Engineering Software in the Age of AI</h3>
          <div class="writing-card-copy">
            <p>AI is making software easier to build. But is it making software better engineered?</p>
            <p>Introducing <strong>TechBook</strong>, the first LAB project, where I explore modern AI engineering through four disciplines: <strong>Define clearly. Design deliberately. Deliver with understanding. Defend relentlessly.</strong></p>
            <p>As AI takes on more of the coding, the real challenge shifts to maintaining clarity, control, understanding and trust.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="writing-card-link" href={site.techbookArticle} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the article on Substack <ArrowUpRight size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
